---
import type { HomeProps } from "#/themes/types";
import Layout from "./Layout.astro";

Astro.props as HomeProps;
---

<Layout
  title="jwstn.dev — JW, full-stack developer in Cologne"
  description="JW is a full-stack developer in Cologne building web applications with TanStack, occasionally wandering into Effect — and carrying a camera, most recently through Japan."
>
  <section class="eth-hero eth-fade">
    <p class="eth-kicker">JW — Full-Stack Developer — Cologne</p>
    <h1 class="eth-display">
      Built quietly,<br />
      <em>kept like light in the mist.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="eth-lede">
      I'm JW, a full-stack developer in Cologne. Most of my days go into web applications with
      <a href="https://tanstack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TanStack</a> — it quietly
      covers so much of what a modern app needs that
      <a href="https://hono.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hono</a> and
      <a href="https://elysiajs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Elysia</a> are still
      waiting their turn on the shelf. What I did make room for is
      <a href="https://effect.website/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Effect</a> — the most
      fun I've had in a while, and a whole new way to think about writing a program.
    </p>
    <p class="eth-lede">
      When the keyboard rests, the camera comes out. In 2026 it travelled to Japan — and it hasn't
      really been put away since.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="eth-mistline eth-fade" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <section class="eth-doorways eth-fade eth-fade-2" aria-labelledby="eth-doorways-h">
    <h2 id="eth-doorways-h" class="eth-kicker">Where to wander</h2>
    <div class="eth-doorway-grid">
      <a class="eth-panel eth-doorway" href="/projects">
        <span class="eth-doorway-kicker">Projects</span>
        <span class="eth-doorway-title">Four small lights, still burning</span>
        <span class="eth-doorway-note">
          Works in slow progress — a home for vinyl collections, a terminal that plays music, a way to
          learn sign-language, and a note app that is entirely mine.
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="eth-panel eth-doorway" href="/blog">
        <span class="eth-doorway-kicker">Blog</span>
        <span class="eth-doorway-title">Nothing has drifted in yet</span>
        <span class="eth-doorway-note">
          Words take their time here. Something is gathering — it will arrive when it stops moving.
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="eth-panel eth-doorway" href="/gallery">
        <span class="eth-doorway-kicker">Gallery</span>
        <span class="eth-doorway-title">Photographs, kept soft</span>
        <span class="eth-doorway-note">
          Japan 2026, a German summer, and the spring that opened the year — kept like pressed
          flowers.
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
